Assertions:
[NAV] Browser navigates to {picked_pdp_url}
[DOM] PDP page heading text contains {picked_pdp_name}
[STATE] Search dropdown closes after product click
[DOM] PDP renders product image, price, and primary action (qty stepper or Add-to-Cart) — no broken placeholders

Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
- Browser viewport resized to 375px width (iPhone SE)
- Storefront accessible at {{FRONT_URL}}

Steps:
[NAV] Navigate to {{FRONT_URL}}
[SETUP] read test-data/search-queries/b2b-buyer-queries.csv, filter rows where query_type=brand-in-query, pick a random row → {picked_query}; extract the brand token (first word) → {brand_token}; extract the noun token (remaining words) → {noun_token}
[LOG] write {picked_query, brand_token, noun_token} to evidence
[ACT] Click the search input
[ACT] fill 'Search': {picked_query}
[KEY] press [Enter]
[WAIT] Wait for /search?q=… results page to load
[SETUP] browser_snapshot the results grid; capture the first product card's visible name → {first_card_name}; count how many of the top 5 cards' names contain {brand_token} (case-insensitive) → {brand_hit_count}
[LOG] append {first_card_name, brand_hit_count} to evidence
[ASSERT] Verify at least 1 product card is rendered
[ASSERT] Verify {first_card_name} contains either {brand_token} OR {noun_token} (a brand-only or noun-only hit is acceptable; a card with neither indicates the search engine ignored both tokens)
[ASSERT] Verify {brand_hit_count} >= 1 in the top 5 (the brand token is ranked into the top results, not buried)

[NAV] Navigate to {{FRONT_URL}}
[SETUP] read test-data/search-queries/b2b-buyer-queries.csv, filter rows where query_type=color-in-query, pick a random row → {picked_query}; extract the color token (first word) → {color_token}; extract the noun token (remaining words) → {noun_token}
[LOG] write {picked_query, color_token, noun_token} to evidence
[ACT] Click the search input
[ACT] fill 'Search': {picked_query}
[KEY] press [Enter]
[WAIT] Wait for /search?q=… results page to load
[SETUP] browser_snapshot the results grid; capture the first card's name → {first_card_name}; if a Color facet is present in the sidebar, capture whether {color_token} appears as a facet value → {color_in_facet}
[LOG] append {first_card_name, color_in_facet} to evidence
[ASSERT] Verify at least 1 product card is rendered (NOT zero — color+noun should not return empty)
[ASSERT] Verify {first_card_name} contains {noun_token} (the product-type semantics carried through)
[ASSERT] Verify either: {first_card_name} contains {color_token} (color is in the product name) OR the Color facet shows {color_token} as a value (color matched via attribute) — pick whichever the storefront supports

[NAV] Navigate to {{FRONT_URL}}
[ACT] Open the main catalog navigation menu
[ASSERT] browser_snapshot the nav; pick a top-level category link that has visible subcategories → click it → store its name as {parent_category_name}
[WAIT] Category page loads and search bar scope indicator settles
[ASSERT] browser_snapshot the category page (sidebar or sub-nav); pick a child/subcategory link → click it → store its name as {child_category_name}
[WAIT] Child category page loads; search bar scope chip settles naming {child_category_name}
[SETUP] `browser_evaluate` (read-only DOM instrumentation, installed BEFORE the breadcrumb click so the ~161-381ms transient loading window is never missed — a MutationObserver queues every DOM/attribute change in order regardless of main-thread load; an earlier requestAnimationFrame sampler was tried and discarded because it starves exactly when the route change happens, so it can report zero violations without ever having observed the loading state): const c=document.querySelector('.search-bar .vc-input__decorator'); const inp=document.querySelector('[data-test-id=global-search-query-input]'); window.__srchTimeline=[]; const snap=()=>{ const chips=c?Array.from(c.querySelectorAll('[data-search-scope]')):[]; const loadingCount=c?Array.from(c.children).filter(el=>!el.matches('[data-search-scope]')).length:0; window.__srchTimeline.push({t:performance.now(), loadingCount, chipCount:chips.length, chipLabels:chips.map(el=>(el.querySelector('.vc-button__slot')?.textContent||el.getAttribute('data-search-scope')||'').trim()), placeholder:inp?inp.getAttribute('placeholder'):null, neighborX:inp?inp.getBoundingClientRect().left:null}); }; snap(); const mo1=new MutationObserver(snap); if(c) mo1.observe(c,{childList:true,subtree:true,characterData:true}); const mo2=new MutationObserver(snap); if(inp) mo2.observe(inp,{attributes:true,attributeFilter:['placeholder']}); window.__srchObservers=[mo1,mo2]; return {installed:true, baseline:window.__srchTimeline[0]}; — confirm installed===true
[LOG] write {parent_category_name, child_category_name} to evidence
[ACT] Click the breadcrumb link labeled "{parent_category_name}" in the breadcrumb trail
[WAIT] Wait for the parent category page and scope indicator to fully settle (a real user click, not a reload — the observers installed above persist across this SPA route change)
[SETUP] `browser_evaluate` (read-only replay of the recorded timeline now that the transition has settled — disconnect the observers first so the array is frozen): window.__srchObservers?.forEach(o=>o.disconnect()); const tl=window.__srchTimeline||[]; const inp=document.querySelector('[data-test-id=global-search-query-input]'); const finalNeighborX=inp?inp.getBoundingClientRect().left:null; const baselineX=tl[0]?tl[0].neighborX:null; const maxSimultaneous=tl.reduce((m,e)=>Math.max(m,(e.loadingCount>=1&&e.chipCount>=1)?(e.loadingCount+e.chipCount):0),0); const maxNeighborDelta=baselineX==null?null:tl.reduce((m,e)=>Math.max(m,Math.abs((e.neighborX??baselineX)-baselineX)),0); const settled=tl[tl.length-1]||{}; return {timeline:tl, maxSimultaneous, maxNeighborDelta, finalNeighborX, settledLoadingCount:settled.loadingCount, settledChipCount:settled.chipCount, settledChipLabels:settled.chipLabels}; — store maxSimultaneous as {max_simultaneous}, maxNeighborDelta as {max_neighbor_delta}, settledLoadingCount as {settled_loading_count}, settledChipCount as {settled_chip_count}, settledChipLabels as {settled_chip_labels}, and the full timeline as {scope_timeline} (evidence only)

Assertions:
[DOM] {max_simultaneous} === 0 — across every recorded mutation in {scope_timeline}, the loading indicator and a scope chip were never present together in the scope-indicator slot {SPEC}
[DOM] {settled_chip_count} === 1 AND {settled_loading_count} === 0 AND {settled_chip_labels} contains {parent_category_name} — exactly one scope chip visible at settle, naming {parent_category_name}, with no loading indicator present {SPEC}
[STATE] No loading indicator remains once the scope chip for {parent_category_name} has settled — the last entry recorded in {scope_timeline} has loadingCount 0 {SPEC}

Steps:
[NAV] Navigate to {{FRONT_URL}}
[ACT] Open the main catalog navigation menu
[ASSERT] browser_snapshot the nav; pick a top-level category link that has visible subcategories → click it → store its name as {parent_category_name}
[WAIT] Category page loads
[ASSERT] browser_snapshot the category page; pick a child/subcategory link → click it → store its name as {child_category_name}
[WAIT] Child category page loads; search input placeholder settles
[ASSERT] Read the search input's placeholder text/attribute after settle → store as {baseline_placeholder}
[LOG] write {parent_category_name, child_category_name, baseline_placeholder} to evidence
[SETUP] `browser_evaluate` (read-only DOM instrumentation, installed BEFORE the breadcrumb click so the transient loading window — previously unobservable because browser_click only returns after Playwright settles the navigation — is never missed — a MutationObserver queues every DOM/attribute change in order regardless of main-thread load; an earlier requestAnimationFrame sampler was tried and discarded because it starves exactly when the route change happens, so it can report zero violations without ever having observed the loading state): const c=document.querySelector('.search-bar .vc-input__decorator'); const inp=document.querySelector('[data-test-id=global-search-query-input]'); window.__srchTimeline=[]; const snap=()=>{ const chips=c?Array.from(c.querySelectorAll('[data-search-scope]')):[]; const loadingCount=c?Array.from(c.children).filter(el=>!el.matches('[data-search-scope]')).length:0; window.__srchTimeline.push({t:performance.now(), loadingCount, chipCount:chips.length, chipLabels:chips.map(el=>(el.querySelector('.vc-button__slot')?.textContent||el.getAttribute('data-search-scope')||'').trim()), placeholder:inp?inp.getAttribute('placeholder'):null, neighborX:inp?inp.getBoundingClientRect().left:null}); }; snap(); const mo1=new MutationObserver(snap); if(c) mo1.observe(c,{childList:true,subtree:true,characterData:true}); const mo2=new MutationObserver(snap); if(inp) mo2.observe(inp,{attributes:true,attributeFilter:['placeholder']}); window.__srchObservers=[mo1,mo2]; return {installed:true, baseline:window.__srchTimeline[0]}; — confirm installed===true
[ACT] Click the breadcrumb link labeled "{parent_category_name}" in the breadcrumb trail
[WAIT] Wait for the parent category page and scope state to fully settle (a real user click, not a reload — the observers installed above persist across this SPA route change)
[SETUP] `browser_evaluate` (read-only replay of the recorded timeline now that the transition has settled — disconnect the observers first so the array is frozen; substitute the real captured child-category text for staleName before calling the tool): window.__srchObservers?.forEach(o=>o.disconnect()); const tl=window.__srchTimeline||[]; const inp=document.querySelector('[data-test-id=global-search-query-input]'); const finalNeighborX=inp?inp.getBoundingClientRect().left:null; const staleName='{child_category_name}'; const loadingEntries=tl.filter(e=>e.loadingCount>=1); const staleLeakCount=loadingEntries.filter(e=>(e.placeholder||'').includes(staleName)).length; const nonGenericDuringLoadCount=loadingEntries.filter(e=>(e.placeholder||'')!=='Search').length; const settled=tl[tl.length-1]||{}; return {timeline:tl, loadingEntryCount:loadingEntries.length, staleLeakCount, nonGenericDuringLoadCount, loadingPlaceholders:loadingEntries.map(e=>e.placeholder), settledPlaceholder:settled.placeholder, finalNeighborX}; — store loadingEntryCount as {loading_entry_count}, staleLeakCount as {stale_leak_count}, nonGenericDuringLoadCount as {non_generic_during_load_count}, settledPlaceholder as {settled_placeholder}, and the full timeline as {scope_timeline} (evidence only)

Assertions:
[DOM] {baseline_placeholder} contains '{child_category_name}' (sanity check — scoped placeholder works on the initial settled state) {SPEC}
[DOM] {stale_leak_count} === 0 — no recorded state where a loading indicator was present ever showed the placeholder containing the stale (previous) category name {SPEC}
[DOM] {non_generic_during_load_count} === 0 — every recorded state where a loading indicator was present shows the generic 'Search' placeholder, never a category name {SPEC}
[DOM] {settled_placeholder} contains '{parent_category_name}' — the placeholder names the NEW settled category, not the stale one and not the generic text {SPEC}
[STATE] The placeholder only ever names a category once the scope has settled — {loading_entry_count} === 0 OR {non_generic_during_load_count} === 0 confirms every loading-window entry stayed on the generic placeholder {SPEC}

Steps:
[NAV] Navigate to {{FRONT_URL}}
[ACT] Open the main catalog navigation menu
[ASSERT] browser_snapshot the nav; pick a top-level category link that has visible subcategories → click it → store its name as {parent_category_name}
[WAIT] Category page loads
[ASSERT] browser_snapshot the category page; pick a child/subcategory link → click it → store its name as {child_category_name}
[WAIT] Child category page loads; search bar scope chip settles naming {child_category_name}
