Assertions:
[DOM] After the category-to-category navigation settles, the scope chip for {parent_category_name} exposes a remove/clear control that is visible and clickable {SPEC}
[STATE] Clicking the remove control clears the category scope — the chip is removed from the search bar {SPEC}
[DOM] After the scope clears, no category name is present in the search input placeholder — it returns to the generic keyword-entry text {SPEC}
[STATE] The remove control is never permanently unreachable after a category-to-category navigation — i.e. the loading-state flag governing the chip's v-else branch always resolves back to false, even after a prior navigation {SPEC}
